  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "The heartbeat of a quartz watch",
    "kn": "ಕ್ವಾರ್ಟ್ಸ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರದ ಹೃದಯಬಡಿತ"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "A quartz watch loses only a few seconds a month. Inside it a tiny slice of quartz vibrates at 32 768 times a second, held steady by its own mechanical resonance.",
    "kn": "ಕ್ವಾರ್ಟ್ಸ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರ ತಿಂಗಳಿಗೆ ಕೆಲವೇ ಸೆಕೆಂಡು ತಪ್ಪುತ್ತದೆ. ಅದರೊಳಗಿನ ಸಣ್ಣ ಕ್ವಾರ್ಟ್ಸ್ ತುಂಡು ಸೆಕೆಂಡಿಗೆ 32 768 ಬಾರಿ ಕಂಪಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Explain the piezoelectric effect"
    },
    {
     "en": "Draw the equivalent circuit of a crystal"
    },
    {
     "en": "Explain why crystal oscillators are so stable"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A quartz watch loses only a few seconds a month. Inside it a tiny slice of quartz vibrates at 32 768 times a second, held steady by its own mechanical resonance.",
    "kn": "ಕ್ವಾರ್ಟ್ಸ್ ಗಡಿಯಾರ ತಿಂಗಳಿಗೆ ಕೆಲವೇ ಸೆಕೆಂಡು ತಪ್ಪುತ್ತದೆ. ಅದರೊಳಗಿನ ಸಣ್ಣ ಕ್ವಾರ್ಟ್ಸ್ ತುಂಡು ಸೆಕೆಂಡಿಗೆ 32 768 ಬಾರಿ ಕಂಪಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Piezoelectric effect"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Some crystals such as quartz, Rochelle salt and tourmaline show the piezoelectric effect: mechanical stress across two faces produces a voltage, and a voltage applied across them produces a mechanical strain. An AC voltage therefore makes the crystal vibrate, and the vibration is strongest at the crystal's natural (mechanical resonant) frequency. This frequency depends on the cut and size of the slice and is inversely proportional to its thickness. Quartz is used because it is mechanically strong, cheap and very stable with temperature."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Stress ⇄ voltage (piezoelectric effect)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Quartz, Rochelle salt, tourmaline"
    },
    {
     "en": "Natural frequency ∝ 1/thickness"
    },
    {
     "en": "Quartz: strong, cheap, temperature-stable"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In the piezoelectric effect, pressing a crystal produces a voltage and a voltage makes it vibrate. A thinner crystal vibrates at a higher frequency.",
    "kn": "ಪೀಜೋಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಿಕ್ ಪರಿಣಾಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ಫಟಿಕವನ್ನು ಒತ್ತಿದರೆ ವೋಲ್ಟೇಜ್ ಉಂಟಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ವೋಲ್ಟೇಜ್ ನೀಡಿದರೆ ಅದು ಕಂಪಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ತೆಳುವಾದ ಸ್ಫಟಿಕ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಆವೃತ್ತಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಕಂಪಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
